## Claim
Text: "The Wire called Durga puja racist and the goddess Durga a sex worker"
Claim date: October 26, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did the news organization "The Wire" publish an article, video, or report between January 1, 2020, and October 26, 2020, that explicitly labeled the Hindu festival "Durga Puja" as "racist"?
Answer: No, The Wire did not publish any article explicitly labeling Durga Puja as "racist" between January 1, 2020, and October 26, 2020. The claim is based on a misrepresented 2016 article that quoted then-HRD Minister Smriti Irani reading excerpts from a disputed JNU pamphlet during a parliamentary speech.

Source URL: https://www.altnews.in/the-wire-did-not-disrespect-durga-excerpt-from-2016-article-misrepresented/

### In the same or another publication from "The Wire" during that period, did it explicitly refer to the Hindu goddess "Durga" as a "sex worker"?
Answer: No, The Wire did not explicitly refer to the goddess Durga as a "sex worker" in its own voice. The search result from The Quint clarifies that the controversial excerpt was a direct quotation from Union Minister Smriti Irani's speech in Parliament, where she read from a pamphlet she alleged was distributed at JNU. The Wire's article was reporting on that speech and quoted her words, but the characterization originated from the pamphlet content, not from The Wire itself.

