### Justification
The fact-check reveals that the viral claim misrepresents a 2016 [report by The Wire](https://thewire.in/92853/smriti-irani-reads-out-obscene-verse-in-lok-sabha-to-show-jnu-event-was-not-about-culture/) covering a parliamentary speech by then-HRD Minister Smriti Irani, who read excerpts from a controversial pamphlet. The statements about Durga being a "sex worker" and Durga Puja being "racist" were direct quotations from that pamphlet, not The Wire’s own editorial stance, as confirmed by multiple fact-checkers ([Alt News](https://www.altnews.in/the-wire-did-not-disrespect-durga-excerpt-from-2016-article-misrepresented/), [The Quint](https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/excerpt-shared-without-context-to-label-the-wire-as-anti-hindu), [The Logical Indian](https://thelogicalindian.com/fact-check/wire-demeans-goddess-durga-24521)). The Wire’s founding editor also clarified that the article was quoting the speech, not endorsing the content, and that the screenshot was taken out of context.